===========================================================================
VERDICT: PARTIAL -- ARP learning PROVEN; "full tables" NOT MEASURABLE here.
===========================================================================

PROVEN -- and this is the useful result:
  **The DUT does not learn ARP entries from unsolicited (gratuitous) ARP.**
      6000 gratuitous ARP replies from 6000 distinct sender IP/MAC pairs on an
      on-link 10.90.0.0/16 secondary subnet  ->  0 entries in `show arp`
  Learning from the DUT's OWN resolution works normally:
      ping 10.38.215.33  ->  2/2, and immediately:
      10.38.215.33  00f0.4d00.7717  vlan1  port2.0.2  dynamic
  So the empty table is not a broken display -- it is the DUT correctly
  declining to populate its cache from unsolicited ARP, which is the
  anti-poisoning behaviour you want.

PROVEN -- stability under the flood:
  after 13000 gratuitous ARPs in total the DUT still resolved and pinged a real
  neighbour 3/3, and the stack stayed `Normal operation` throughout.

NOT MEASURABLE -- "with full tables":
  The table cannot be FILLED from this bench. Because the DUT only learns from
  its own resolutions, filling requires thousands of addresses that actually
  answer ARP. There is one host NIC on the ingress port and no responder
  population, so the fill condition the case names cannot be created.
  A traffic generator emulating thousands of live hosts (the ixia the other
  cases assume) would close this.

  Also noted: `show arp counter` is NOT supported on this build
  ("% Invalid input"). `show arp` and `show arp global` both work and were used
  instead.

CASE NOTE: AWPTCM-T6057 has num_steps = 0 in ck.db, so the shape above is my
interpretation of the title, stated explicitly rather than implied.
